  "id": "endoplasmic-reticulum",
  "term": "endoplasmic reticulum",
  "definition": "The endoplasmic reticulum is a network-like structure inside eukaryotic cells that helps make, process, and transport proteins and also supports lipid and sterol production. When cell conditions disrupt normal protein folding, stress responses in the endoplasmic reticulum are activated to restore balance, but prolonged severe stress can lead to cell death.",
